WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.370
Machine knitters will often scrap off
their knitting and rehang the stitches.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.400
This is equivalent to putting stitches
on a holder and hand knitting

00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:12.930
to temporarily pause your knitting.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.890
You might scrap off and rehang to turn
the work and knit some purl rows,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.480
or you might scrap off some shoulder
stitches on a sweater and then rehang

00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:27.770
those stitches of both
shoulders to join the seam.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.650
Scrapping off is just knitting a few
rows with the contrasting color yarn.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.880
Now, if your yarn isn't slippery or
the piece isn't going to be handled a lot,

00:00:36.946 --> 00:00:39.690
it isn't necessary to bind off the scrap.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.090
Just drop the knitting from the machine.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.050
When it's time to rehang the knitting
on the machine,

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.290
start by putting the required number
of needles into working position.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.650
To make things easier, open the latches.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.090
I'm just using the edge
of a business card.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.450
Use a single or double
prong transfer tool.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.440
Ignore the scrap, in this case the blue
yarn, and put the tool

00:01:04.506 --> 00:01:06.130
in the garment stitches.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.810
In this case, the pink stitches.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:15.610
Next, hang the eye of the tool over the
hooks of the needles on the needle bed.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.530
Lift the tool and slip those stitches
off the tool and onto the needles.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.130
Make sure you haven't caught any
of that scrap yarn or split the stitches.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.330
Repeat this until all the required
stitches are back on the machine.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
Now, you can remove the scrap right now
and confirm your pickup or leave

00:01:37.346 --> 00:01:40.930
the scrap in place, just in case.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Picking up stitches from scrap is
an essential skill that will become

00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:47.400
second nature the more you work it.

